Exact interleaving, starting with Alice and Bob both on call:
1. Alice begins at repeatable read and counts 2, establishing her snapshot.
2. Bob begins at repeatable read and counts 2, establishing his snapshot before Alice commits.
3. Alice updates only Alice to off call. Her transaction sees Bob still on call.
4. Bob updates only Bob to off call. His snapshot still sees Alice on call.
5. Alice commits; the committed state is Alice off, Bob on.
6. Bob commits; the committed state is Alice off, Bob off. Neither updated a row changed by the other, so both updates can succeed.

