**Addition order and coverage.** The offsets are 16, 8, 4, 2, 1. At each stage, a lane adds its current partial sum to its partner’s pre-stage partial sum, using round-to-nearest float addition. Initially lane ℓ contains only input ℓ. After processing a set of offsets, its expression contains precisely the inputs indexed by ℓ plus subset sums of those offsets, restricted to indices below 19. The next offset creates two disjoint sets: subsets excluding that offset and subsets including it. Distinct subsets have distinct sums because the offsets are distinct powers of two. If the partner is outside 0–18, every index in its prospective set is also outside, so skipping the addition loses no input. After all five stages, lane 0 therefore contains every input 0–18 exactly once. The final shuffle delivers that same rounded result to every caller.

**Participation and synchronization.** Every source is either a partner below 19 or the calling lane itself, so its bit is set in `0x0007ffffu` and it participates. All 19 lanes execute the same five reduction shuffles and final broadcast with the same mask and width 32, including lanes with no partner. The synchronized collectives exchange each stage’s register values without assuming implicit lockstep; no shared-memory synchronization is needed. A self-read cannot double-count anything because `has_partner` is false and the addition is skipped.

Finite inputs do not guarantee finite intermediate sums: float overflow can occur, and opposite-signed infinities can subsequently produce NaN. The guarantee is exact-once input coverage in the specified floating-point addition expression, not an exact real-arithmetic sum.

Use one fold shuffle, four butterfly shuffles, and one redistribution shuffle using three distinct completed sums—not a final broadcast from one lane. All 19 callers execute exactly six float shuffles.

```cpp
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

__device__ __forceinline__ float sum19(float value)
{
    const unsigned int rank =
        threadIdx.x + blockDim.x *
        (threadIdx.y + blockDim.y * threadIdx.z);
    const unsigned int lane = rank % 32u;
    constexpr unsigned int mask = 0x0007ffffu;

    // Fold inputs 16, 17, 18 into lanes 0, 1, 2.
    const int fold_source = static_cast<int>(
        lane < 3u ? lane + 16u : lane);
    const float extra = __shfl_sync(mask, value, fold_source, 32);
    float sum = value;
    if (lane < 3u) {
        sum = __fadd_rn(sum, extra);
    }

    // Butterfly all-reduction of the 16 folded values.
    for (unsigned int distance = 1u; distance <= 8u;
         distance <<= 1u) {
        const int source = static_cast<int>(
            lane < 16u ? (lane ^ distance) : lane);
        const float other = __shfl_sync(mask, sum, source, 32);
        if (lane < 16u) {
            sum = __fadd_rn(sum, other);
        }
    }

    // Extra lanes read completed sums from three distinct lanes.
    const int result_source = static_cast<int>(
        lane >= 16u ? lane - 16u : lane);
    return __shfl_sync(mask, sum, result_source, 32);
}
